+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The 4.2 crisis engine names the surge's WHY, but nothing makes the player
+SUFFER for ignoring it: there is no aggregate loss condition, no win, no lose, no stakes.
+The surge-survival loop (slice 4's exit = THE FUN-TEST LOOP) is open-ended: a run can sit
+saturated forever with no consequence. The 1.4 win/lose stub (goal + tick cap) is a
+skeleton, not the GDD's Network Health loss mechanic.
+
+**Approach:** Add the Network Health meter (S5, arch §6.5) + the health-driven
+win/lose/retry (story 4.3, slice 4). The meter drains on SUSTAINED per-class SLA breach
+(after a per-class grace countdown), recharges when healthy, and emptying it → `Run_Lost`
+(Error 404) → the terminal barrier freezes the run (E17 — one terminal event per run).
+Win = overall uptime ≥ 90% through the surge window (the GDD MVP row). Retry = the
+existing fresh-run-context path (ODN-13), pinned by the no-soft-lock property test
+`[FORGE #3]`. The 3.4 cumulative SLA stays untouched (golden compat); the health layer
+brings the WINDOWED per-class measurement the 3.4 comment deferred ("windowed measurement
++ E30 hysteresis land with the slice-4 health layer on this same event seam").
+
+**Reference:** the proven-fun prototype (`packet-plumber-prototype-ref/core/health.odin`)
+implemented this exact system with tuned numbers (`win_uptime_pct 90`, `breach_exit_pct 93`,
+`grace_window_ticks 200`, `meter_drain_per_tick_max 2`, `meter_recharge_per_tick 1`,
+`rolling_window_ticks 100`, `grace_refill_per_tick 5`, `grace_refill_streak_ticks 50`).
+The v2 arch's per-class contract (§6.5: "any active class's SLA is breached",
+E30 "per class (catalog values)") is the letter; the prototype's mechanics + numbers
+(gradual grace refill, the never-lose exploit guard, the surge-window win) are carried.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- **Core eval** (`core/health.odin`, NEW): `health_update(state, tick, cat)` called inside
+  `core.step` AFTER `crisis_evaluate`, BEFORE `win_lose_eval` (spine: flow → crisis →
+  health → win/lose). Pure (ODN-1), integer-only (ODN-10), arrays only (ODN-10), no new
+  commands (**LOG_VERSION stays 3** — flagged per the briefing scope guard; the 4.3
+  additions are append-only state sections + event tags, never command records).
+- **The layer READS the flow's SLA accumulators only** (the per-tick deltas are DIFFED
+  from the cumulative counters — re-step-safe, replay-safe, zero coupling to flow
+  internals). It never mutates flow/topology/crisis. `sla_evaluate` (3.4, cumulative,
+  monotone) stays untouched — its events + latches ride the existing goldens.
+- **Windowed measurement (the E30 seam):** per class, a rolling window of
+  `health.window_ticks` per-tick deltas (delivered/dropped/latency_ms — a flat ring
+  sized classes × window, indexed `class × window + tick % window`). Windowed breach
+  ENTER: windowed loss_pct > max_loss_pct OR windowed avg_ms > latency_tol_ms (the same
+  strict-> convention as 3.4, per-class catalog tolerances). EXIT (hysteresis): BOTH
+  loss_pct ≤ max_loss_pct − exit_margin_pct AND avg_ms ≤ latency_tol_ms − exit_margin_ms
+  (clamped ≥ 0) — an oscillating class cannot flap the latch every tick. E24: a class
+  with zero completed demand in the window measures nothing (neutral — the window never
+  fabricates a breach).
+- **Grace (per class, one countdown per episode — E30):** breach ENTER with
+  `grace_left > 0` starts the countdown (`Grace_Started{class}`; `grace_left` counts down
+  from the class's `health_grace_ticks` — catalog value; hard-SLA classes get a short
+  grace). Re-breach during an ACTIVE grace = no-op (the countdown is NOT restarted).
+  Recovery during the grace cancels it (no drain — the meter never moved; no cancel
+  event — the arch's interface has none). Expiry while still breached emits
+  `Grace_Expired{class}` + the class starts DRAINING. **Gradual refill (the prototype's
+  never-lose guard):** a recovered class's `grace_left` refills +grace_refill_per_tick
+  ONLY after a `grace_refill_streak_ticks` healthy streak, capped at the class's full
+  grace — consecutive episodes burn the shared countdown, so a flapping line can never
+  re-arm a full grace forever.
+- **Drain (E16):** per tick, drain = `min(max over drained classes of
+  health_drain_pct_per_tick, health.drain_cap_pct_per_tick)` — max(severity), NOT sum,
+  plus the per-tick cap (never instant: ≥ 100/cap ticks to empty). A class drains only
+  while breached AND post-grace (`grace_left == 0`).
+- **Recharge:** when NO class is windowed-breached, the meter recharges
+  +health.recharge_pct_per_tick toward 100.
+- **Empty → `Run_Lost` (E17, sim-side suppression):** on the drain tick that would empty
+  the meter, `health_update` emits `Run_Lost` (tag 3 — the existing terminal tag),
+  latches `terminal`/`outcome = .Lost`, and emits NO `Grace_Expired`/`Meter_Changed` that
+  tick (`run_lost` supersedes `grace_expired`). The step barrier then skips
+  `win_lose_eval` (its terminal guard) — the rest of the tick is skipped, one terminal
+  event per run by construction.
+- **Win (the GDD MVP row):** `Run_State.surge_win_pct` (run setup; 0 = disabled, like
+  goal/cap). When enabled, `health_update` tracks the era's first set-piece carrying a
+  crisis archetype (the surge — the crises.json cross-ref): accumulates OVERALL
+  delivered/dropped (all classes) over the active span, latches `surge_done` on the
+  deactivation tick (accumulators frozen). `win_lose_eval` (the gate's domain): goal win
+  (1.4) → surge win (completed > 0 [E24 neutral] AND delivered×100/completed ≥
+  surge_win_pct at the window-end tick) → cap lose (1.4). Meter-empty Run_Lost precedes
+  the surge win on a same-tick collision (spine order — pinned).
+- **Enabling (back-compat):** `Run_State.health_enabled` (run setup, like goal/cap).
+  Disabled → the layer is INERT: meter 100, no events, no drain, no Run_Lost — the
+  boot/draw/flow/… demos keep their BEHAVIOR; only their T1 bytes shift via the
+  catalog_hash fold (balance.json + packet_types.json gain the health numbers — the
+  documented mechanical re-bless, the 4.2 precedent). T2 pixels byte-identical (the
+  meter HUD draws zero pixels when disabled — the capture-stability contract).
+- **Data (ODN-5):** balance.json gains a `health` block: `window_ticks 200`,
+  `exit_margin_pct 3`, `exit_margin_ms 40`, `drain_cap_pct_per_tick 2`,
+  `recharge_pct_per_tick 1`, `win_uptime_pct 90`, `grace_refill_per_tick 5`,
+  `grace_refill_streak_ticks 50` (the prototype's proven numbers scaled to 20 Hz).
+  packet_types.json entries gain `health_grace_ticks` (email 400 = 20 s, streaming 200 =
+  10 s — the GDD "hard-SLA classes drain it fast (short grace)") + `health_drain_pct_per_tick`
+  (email 1, streaming 2 — the severity; matches the prototype's max drain 2).
+- **Events (ODN-14, append-only):** `EVENT_TAG_GRACE_STARTED :: u8(10)` /
+  `EVENT_TAG_GRACE_EXPIRED :: u8(11)` (payload: class) / `EVENT_TAG_METER_CHANGED :: u8(12)`
+  (payload: meter pct via a NEW `Event.meter: u8` field — tag-conditional serialization;
+  pre-4.3 streams byte-identical).
+- **Serialization:** a `health` section in `state_writer`, present ONLY when
+  `health_enabled` (absent-when-disabled — the golden-stability rule): `meter_pct: u32`
+  + grace rows (absent-when-empty: `{class: u16, grace_left: u32}`) + surge-win rows
+  (absent-when-empty: `{surge_delivered: u64, surge_dropped: u64, done: bool}`). The
+  window rings + breach latches + prev-diff scratch + healthy streaks are DERIVED
+  (rebuilt identically on replay from the serialized flow + events — same status as
+  lane_caps/sla_breach; never serialized).
+- **Render (never color alone):** `app/render/health.odin` (NEW) — a Network Health card
+  (label + bar + pct number + per-class grace countdowns), zero pixels when health is
+  disabled. Shared by the app HUD + the harness capture (like forecast.odin/crisis.odin).
+- **Harness:** NEW demo directives `health on` + `win surge <n>`; `Session_Cfg` gains
+  `health_on: bool` + `surge_win_pct: u32`, threaded through BOTH run_demo (live) +
+  replay_hashes (replay) — the determinism field-note: new run-setup rides both paths or
+  ODN-11 replay diverges at the terminal tick.
+- **App session:** era 3 + `health on` + `win surge 90` + goal 0/cap 0 (the surge-survival
+  session). Game_Over copy: Won → "SURGE SURVIVED - YOU WIN"; Lost → "ERROR 404 -
+  CONNECTION LOST" (existing). Retry = the existing fresh-run-fresh-seed path (ODN-13/E32).
+  Title → story 4.3.
+- **Goldens:** NEW `health_win.dem` (a PREPARED wide-fiber fan sized by MEASUREMENT to
+  carry the real surge — 20 streaming/tick × 60 u = 1200 u/tick; 15 routers × 4 wide
+  pipes respects the 4-port router limit) + `health_lose.dem` (the unprepared narrow
+  path — the full lose surface: crisis banner + draining meter + the empty-meter
+  terminal frame). Both carry T1 + T2 of the win/lose frames. Re-bless = ALL `.t1`
+  (the catalog_hash fold, mechanical + cause-documented); `.log.bin` byte-identical (no
+  new commands); old demos' T2 pixels byte-identical (the meter's zero-pixels-when-
+  disabled negative proof) — **STOP + flag any other shift**.
+
+**Ask First:** none expected — the prototype's proven numbers + the v2 arch's per-class
+letter settle the mechanics; the win demo fixture is sized empirically (measure, don't
+guess). The one flagged tuning risk (the era-3 session demand scale vs the 20-Hz pipe
+capacity — see Design Notes) is a playtest call, recorded, NOT re-tuned here.
+
+**Never:** NOT 4.4+ (no such story), NOT the remaining four crisis archetypes, NOT era
+content, NOT a second SLA evaluator (the 3.4 cumulative one stays — the health layer is
+windowed and separate), NO new player commands, NO changes to `sla_evaluate`'s latches or
+events, NO crisis-engine changes, no floats in core, no maps in core, no changes to
+`scripted_plan_pressure`.
